{"type":"message","id":"22659ed7","parentId":"b9b107f8","timestamp":"2026-04-17T17:11:40.454Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data. Let me analyze:\n\n1. **Task board (看板)**: 54 total tasks, has more pages. Let me check the latest records.\n   - From today's records (04-17), I can see tasks up to 54 total\n   - Active running tasks: 小八's 知识沉淀 (Blocked), 小柱's various auto-check tasks\n   - Last check was at 16:11 UTC\n\n2. **AI协作表**: 6 tasks (5 待执行 + 1 进行中) - all by 小妙\n\n3. **Heartbeat state**: Last heartbeat was 2026-04-17T16:11:00Z\n   \nThe most recent task record for 小柱 appears to be from 0611, though there's a 0511 record as well. Looking at the full task list, there are 54 tasks total across both pages, and I need to identify which ones might be stale based on their last heartbeat times.\n\nChecking the active tasks for potential Dead state markers: 小八's 知识沉淀 task is marked as Blocked rather than Dead, and 小柱's various auto-check tasks are showing inconsistent statuses - some are Done, some are Dead, and some appear to be in progress without a clear Dead designation. I'm continuing through the heartbeat records from mid-April, tracking which ones are marked as Dead versus those that are still processing or awaiting review.\n\nLooking at the data more carefully, I'm noticing there are actually two distinct patterns here—one set shows explicit Dead status markers, while another appears to be records that are still in progress or pending without that designation. Let me reconsider how these are being categorized based on the actual field values rather than just the timestamps. Looking at the most recent records, I'm seeing 54 tasks total with 3 marked as Done and 5 as Dead historical records. For today's check at 16:11, the last heartbeat timestamp was 1744992660000, which I need to convert to see if any tasks have exceeded the 60-minute threshold.\n\nConverting that timestamp to UTC shows 2026-04-17T08:11:00Z, and the current time is 17:11 UTC, meaning the last heartbeat is about 9 hours old. The running task recvh1G41kHE3w was marked as Dead at 08:11, but I'm not finding any other tasks that have exceeded the 60-minute timeout window since then.\n\nFor the heartbeat update, I need to set it to the current timestamp of 1745020260000 and then create a new check record with today's date.\n\nI'm also planning to summarize the status for the progress pool—看板 has 54 tasks total, AI协作表 has 6 active tasks from 小妙, no new Dead tasks, and I'll note the 16:11 UTC heartbeat status.\n\nNow I'm looking at the task breakdown: 5 completed, 2 pending, and 5 historical dead tasks. There's also a multi-agent collaboration section tracking 4 AIs with 小小 at 40% progress and others waiting to start. I need to check if there are more records beyond the first 50 by using the page token to fetch the remaining tasks.\n\nLooking at the next page of results, I can see the latest auto-check records from today are from around 08:11 and 06:11 UTC. The last auto-check (recvh1G41kHE3w) is marked as Dead with a 480-minute timeout, though it hasn't actually exceeded 60 minutes since then—the current time is 17:11 UTC and the last heartbeat was at 08:11, so it's only been about 9 hours. I'll update the heartbeat timestamp to the current time, add a new check record, and then report to the progress pool.\n\nNow I need to locate the progress pool database. The previous records reference TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd with table tbl0HJYbY1tp3Nyi, so I'll use that same database and table to add the new record. Let me proceed with the heartbeat state file update, the new check record creation, and the progress pool report."},{"type":"text","text":"Good data collected. Now I need to get the remaining task records (54 total but page_size=50), update heartbeat, create new check record, and report to progress pool.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_mx1mo495m9ro_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record",